<%# locals: (index:, term: nil) %>
<%#
  One line of the calculation: a base, a rate, and the two independent ways it
  can be narrowed.

  Indexed rather than submitted as a bare array. The builder adds and removes
  rows, and with `terms[][base]` a row deleted from the middle would re-pair
  every base below it with the wrong rate -- silently, and in a form whose
  whole subject is arithmetic.

  The two narrowings are laid out apart from each other because they are
  different questions and get confused constantly. The clock asks how old the
  account is now; the window asks when it was opened. A PEA opened in 2014 is
  both mature and of the 2013-2017 vintage, and those two facts select
  different terms.
%>

<li class="rounded-lg border border-secondary border-xs p-3 space-y-3"
    data-controller="element-removal">
  <div class="grid gap-3 @xl:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="@xl:col-span-5">
      <%= select_tag "tax_rule[terms][#{index}][base]",
                     options_for_select(tax_base_choices, term&.base),
                     include_blank: t(".base_blank"),
                     class: "form-field__input",
                     aria: { label: t(".base_label") } %>
      <p class="text-xs text-subdued mt-1"><%= t(".base_hint") %></p>
    </div>

    <div class="@xl:col-span-4">
      <%= select_tag "tax_rule[terms][#{index}][rate]",
                     options_for_select(tax_rate_choices, term&.rate),
                     include_blank: t(".rate_blank"),
                     class: "form-field__input",
                     aria: { label: t(".rate_label") } %>
      <p class="text-xs text-subdued mt-1"><%= t(".rate_hint") %></p>
    </div>

    <%# Only meaningful when the rate above is "a fixed rate", and left visible
        rather than toggled by script: a box that appears and disappears as you
        change a select is one more thing to get wrong, and the formula already
        says plainly which of the two fields contradicts the other. %>
    <div class="@xl:col-span-3">
      <%= text_field_tag "tax_rule[terms][#{index}][literal_rate]",
                         tax_literal_percent(term),
                         class: "form-field__input",
                         inputmode: "decimal",
                         placeholder: t(".literal_placeholder"),
                         aria: { label: t(".literal_label") } %>
      <p class="text-xs text-subdued mt-1"><%= t(".literal_hint") %></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid gap-3 @xl:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="@xl:col-span-5">
      <%= select_tag "tax_rule[terms][#{index}][condition]",
                     options_for_select(tax_condition_choices, term&.condition || "always"),
                     class: "form-field__input",
                     aria: { label: t(".condition_label") } %>
      <p class="text-xs text-subdued mt-1"><%= t(".condition_hint") %></p>
    </div>

    <div class="@xl:col-span-3">
      <%= date_field_tag "tax_rule[terms][#{index}][opened_from]",
                         term&.opened_from,
                         class: "form-field__input",
                         aria: { label: t(".opened_from_label") } %>
      <p class="text-xs text-subdued mt-1"><%= t(".opened_from_label") %></p>
    </div>

    <div class="@xl:col-span-3">
      <%= date_field_tag "tax_rule[terms][#{index}][opened_until]",
                         term&.opened_until,
                         class: "form-field__input",
                         aria: { label: t(".opened_until_label") } %>
      <p class="text-xs text-subdued mt-1"><%= t(".opened_until_label") %></p>
    </div>

    <div class="@xl:col-span-1 flex items-start justify-end">
      <button type="button"
              class="text-secondary hover:text-destructive p-2"
              data-action="element-removal#remove"
              aria-label="<%= t(".remove") %>">
        <%= icon "trash-2", size: "sm" %>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</li>
